  <title>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Human Security Survey South Sudan (HSS-SS)</narrative>
  </title>
  <description type="1">
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">The HSS is a methodology developed by PAX to better understand and leverage the experiences and perceptions of civilians living in conflict to shape protection policy and practice. With local partners we facilitate dialogues with communities and authorities around the survey findings and identify practical ways to improve the security situation. At the international level, the HSS is used to influence policy providing first-hand information about conflict-affected populations. The survey is continued over multiple years to track trends and work towards sustainable change. In South Sudan, we work in close collaboration with two respected local partners: the Assistance Mission for Africa and the Justice and Peace Commission-Catholic Diocese of Torit.</narrative>
  </description>
